{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis","id":1083179,"title":"Female Mule Fertility and the Perfect Metis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-24T14:24:21-07:00","id":1083179,"title":"Female Mule Fertility and the Perfect Metis","content":"*Opens up Can of Worms*<br /> <br /> *Sacrifices Cat Girl in the name of mixing Fantasy and Science*<br /> <br /> I've been reading about <a href=\"http://messybeast.com/genetics/hybrid-equines.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Mule Infertility</a> and discovered that occasionally a female Mule will give birth to offspring. And sometimes that offspring is a normal horse. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is now known that in most fertile mule mares, the mare passes on a complete set of her maternal genes (i.e. from her horse/pony mother) to the foal rather than a mixture of chromosomes. A female mule bred to a horse will therefore produce a 100% horse foal. </div> </div> </div>Now I am wondering if there have been instances of female metis becoming pregnant and how the Garou Nation would react to such an occurrence. What are the odds of such a pregnancy being allowed to continue or the child/pup surviving to adulthood? <br /> <br /> I am also intrigued by the idea of a Metis mating with the same breed of Kinfolk as their mother producing a normal child/pup. What chance would the offspring go though the first change? Would a Metis/Homid mating still produce a metis? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When a mule gave birth in Albania in 1994, it was thought to have unleashed the spawn of the devil on a small village. When a mule gave birth in 2002 in Morocco five years ago, locals feared it signaled the end of the world. </div> </div> </div>Considering how normal humans reacted to a few mule births, I imagine &quot;metis offspring being the harbinger of the Apocalypse&quot; is not a far fetched response for the Garou. And hey, the &quot;Perfect&quot; metis is considered a harbinger of the Apocalypse. <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, this is all far fetched and will rarely see the light of day at any gaming table, but it doesn't hurt to play the &quot;What if&quot; game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:29:48-07:00","id":1083182,"title":"","content":"Metis aren't physically infertile, they are spiritually so. As in, a male metis has all the equipment and they function just fine, the female metis might menstruate, but idk. They just can't conceive or sire a child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:34:02-07:00","id":1083185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083182#post1083182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metis aren't physically infertile, they are spiritually so. As in, a male metis has all the equipment and they function just fine, the female metis might menstruate, but idk. They just can't conceive or sire a child.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Technically, Male Mules have all the equipment, can mate, but can't sire offspring either. And some Female Mules may have their cycles too.<br /> <br /> I'm really just brainstorming here. I grew up reading scifi, so my mind wanders into dark science places in fantasy/horror settings all the time. I annoy the people in the Exalted forum all the time with comparing the Loom of Fate to Databases and my jokes about Alchemicals running on Linux. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:36:33-07:00","id":1083186,"title":"","content":"If a Apis used &quot;Mercy for the Misbegotten&quot;<br /> How do you think the Garou nation would respond? <br /> <br /> think the child was an abomination, and must be destroyed, <br /> <br /> or a messiah, or what? <br /> <br /> Yes, it might be tinted somewhat by the circumstances of the Apis's return.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:40:08-07:00","id":1083189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083185#post1083185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Technically, Male Mules have all the equipment, can mate, but can't sire offspring either. And some Female Mules may have their cycles too.<br /> <br /> I'm really just brainstorming here. I grew up reading scifi, so my mind wanders into dark science places in fantasy/horror settings all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think what Ana is getting at is that you are sorta comparing apples and oranges, in that horse/donkey hybrids aren't Metis. Biologically speaking, sure, weird things can happen and mules can occasionally breed. In WtA, though, it should take more than just a quirk of genetics for a Metis to have kids. When the First Metis has a child, it actually <i>is</i> a sign of the Apocalypse; it isn't the sort of thing that just happens for no reason other than odd luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 04-24-2017, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:45:33-07:00","id":1083191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083189#post1083189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think what Ana is getting at is that you are sorta comparing apples and oranges, in that horse/donkey hybrids aren't Metis. Biologically speaking, sure, weird things can happen and mules can occasionally breed. In WtA, though, it should take more than just a quirk of genetics for a Metis to have kids. When the First Metis has a child, it actually is a sign of the Apocalypse. It isn't the sort of thing that just happens for no reason other than odd luck.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand I am comparing Apples and Oranges. But I just want to have a thought experiment about what if there was some weird quirk of luck in the past and....<br /> <br /> Bah. Never mind. I guess taking random occurrences and attaching meaning to them would undermine the setting or something like that. <br /> <br /> *collects worms and puts them back into can*<br /> <br /> *throws cat girl corpse onto the fire*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T14:55:54-07:00","id":1083195,"title":"","content":"Also dont forget summer country!<br /> <br /> Metis can have children there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T15:01:35-07:00","id":1083197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083195#post1083195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also dont forget summer country!<br /> <br /> Metis can have children there.</div> </div> </div> </div>What happens in summer country, stays in summer country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T15:14:35-07:00","id":1083200,"title":"","content":"I know, making it truly Bittersweet.<br /> <br /> But think that Mercy for the Misbegotten, could be potentialy misunderstood by the garou enough, that a Returned Apis, wont Casualy use it simply because he's come to like a particular Metis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T08:55:03-07:00","id":1083482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083200#post1083200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, making it truly Bittersweet.<br /> <br /> But think that Mercy for the Misbegotten, could be potentialy misunderstood by the garou enough, that a Returned Apis, wont Casualy use it simply because he's come to like a particular Metis?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be an elder Apis. Impressing them would take an awful lot, and practically no one's heard of them, nor would they suspect to consider a dead Fera as the cause...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:25:52-07:00","id":1083494,"title":"","content":"Would depend how the Apis returned too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:34:12-07:00","id":1083502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083182#post1083182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metis aren't physically infertile, they are spiritually so. As in, a male metis has all the equipment and they function just fine, the female metis might menstruate, but idk. They just can't conceive or sire a child.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metis don't exist in real life. The spiritual/biological differentiation is moot because there's no criteria to convert but our own will.<br /> <br /> So I suggest instead thinking on looser terms. &quot;Mules in our world can produce normal non-mule offspring - What would happen if female metis have a similar potential? Their origin is mule-esque.&quot;<br /> Which is what the OP started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:44:04-07:00","id":1083511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083502#post1083502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Metis don't exist in real life. The spiritual/biological differentiation is moot because there's no criteria to convert but our own will.<br /> <br /> So I suggest instead thinking on looser terms. &quot;Mules in our world can produce normal non-mule offspring - What would happen if female metis have a similar potential? Their origin is mule-esque.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3950_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3950\" data-vbnamecard=\"3950\">wonderandawe</a> stated, kind of undermines the nature of eschatological prophecy. You can disregard that, and have Metis-mating sometimes result in freak pregnancies, but what purpose does that serve? It just means that the Perfect Metis doesn't matter and/or isn't really a thing. Maybe that is fine for your game, but I don't really see how it benefits the setting as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 04-25-2017, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:10:28-07:00","id":1083526,"title":"","content":"He's wondering about adding a little curious detail of mules to the werewolves with a rough parallel.<br /> HOW does it undermine the prophecy? When has humanity ever stopped giving meaning to prophecies just because there's a few &quot;lookalikes&quot; going on?<br /> I'd not be too quick to dismiss that if someone is looking for such appeal. Instead of drawing on an arbitrary disparity to say &quot;no&quot;, let's look at what happens with a &quot;yes&quot;.<br /> <br /> The apocalypse is ALL about that damn prophecy and the chain of events surrounding it. Any time in which &quot;the world is shit&quot; is a valid time for someone watching the freak birth to be alarmed. That's worth a story on its own.<br /> To have part of the nation discrediting the actual perfect metis because it happens a dozen times a century is just as worthy to add to the game if that's your thing.<br /> <br /> It's a layer of complexity in a long and tumultuous endgame.<br /> What do other b\u00eate think of such occurrences? And the spirits? Where do they agree and where do they disagree? How does that play out in an eastern spirit court? Does the metisborn garou inherit the parent's stigma? Has one of them ever chosen to don the mantle of the perfect metis? What went to shit because of that?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:19:18-07:00","id":1083531,"title":"","content":"How are Metis mules? They are the opposite of mules, as both of their parents come from the same species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:22:43-07:00","id":1083533,"title":"","content":"I have thought about it; I am not rejecting the idea out of hand. I dislike the idea not because it is heterodoxy, I dislike it because it turns an auspicious event into a random thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides, even if we discount the Perfect Metis, one of the defining traits of the Metis is their inability to breed: they are cursed by dint of their parent's sin. If this powerful symbol of Gaia's displeasure can be overcome by a random quirk of genetics, it lessens the sting of even being a Metis and discounts the mystic nature of the WtA universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 04-25-2017, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T10:47:14-07:00","id":1083544,"title":"","content":"They're still defined by their inability to breed. Mules are defined in large part by inability to breed.<br /> <br /> That's why the fertile mules are seen as aberrations.<br /> If you add social stigma, they can either be blessed aberrations or aberrations among aberrations.<br /> <br /> Why do you dislike the random factor? We're still talking about something so exceedingly rare it's registered in history but there are few living witnesses of any such event.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:20:04-07:00","id":1083564,"title":"","content":"I'm going to explain my thought process behind why I created this topic and maybe include a funny story.<br /> <br /> A while ago, I saw a topic about a Metis in a romantic relationship with a Mage. Me being a weirdo with an interest in biology wondered &quot;What does a Male Metis semen look like? Are male Metis shooting blanks? Malformed sperm? Sperm that just doesn't recognize human/lupus ovum as a viable destination?&quot; My mind wanders to strange places.<br /> <br /> So I did some research. While Metis aren't mules, they do share the infertility trait with them. I discovered male Mules don't produce sperm at all because of a chromosome mismatch inhibiting the meiosis processes. I doubt the metis has the same exact issue, but its close enough for game psuedo-science. &quot;Cool, let's steal metis shooting blanks in case the question does come up in game.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then I read about Female Mules producing foals. It's a pretty rare event. So rare in countries with a less educated population, they are considered omens. Kind of like how the perfect metis is considered an Omen.<br /> <br /> So, while I agree the general game setting doesn't need any metis producing offspring, the idea of female metis rarely producing offspring may be good story fodder. I would never have a PC metis be fertile. Removing infertility would remove a large part of being metis. I doubt female metis are getting loving any due to the social stigma of metis. The offspring being a product of Rape is a subject I rather not touch upon here. Maybe the Black Spiral Dancers have more incidents of this which would lead to the occasional unholy jihad to bring about the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Any who, I created this topic to brainstorm the Garou Nation's reaction to such events. After a couple of false &quot;Perfect Metis&quot; maybe most Garou discount the actual Perfect Metis. Others could just want to outright kill the offspring. A few true believes may begin to sharpen their claws and klaives in preparation for the upcoming battle. I should disclose I am Agnostic, so religions assigning conflicting meanings to rare and random events intrigues me. My games trend more political, so the Garou arguing over how to react to this &quot;miracle&quot; is good story fodder at my table.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:33:22-07:00","id":1083572,"title":"","content":"So I promised a funny story.<br /> <br /> <b>Child of Gaia: </b> Don't freak out, everyone, but one of our metis tribe members just gave birth.<br /> <b>Uktena:</b> Wait, what? This is a bad omen.<br /> <b>Red Talons:</b> The Apocalypse is upon us.<br /> <b>Get of Fenris:</b> Welp, boys. It's been a good run. Time to prepare for battle of the Apocalypse. *razor claws*<br /> <b>Glasswalker:</b> Are you sure? Did you do any DNA testing?<br /> <b>Black Fury:</b> It's true. I was there for both the mother's birth and the child's birth.<br /> <b>Glasswalker:</b> But did you do any DNA testing?<br /> <b>Silver Fang: </b> Now, we shouldn't get all worked up. I doubt this is the Perfect Metis. My Galliard has stories of other metis births in the past...<br /> <b>Shadow Lord: </b> My Galliard has never heard of such events. What about your Galliards, Fianna?<br /> <b>Fianna:</b> It doesn't matter what the fuck our Galliard's sing. Is unnatural and we should put it down before it falls to the Wyrm.<br /> <b>Child of Gaia: </b>You will NOT lay a hand on this child.<br /> <b>Silent Strider:</b> I wonder who the father is....<br /> <b>Black Fury: </b> The mother didn't say.<br /> <b>Glasswalker: </b> You know a simple DNA test could answer that question.<br /> <b>Black Fury: </b>You are not bringing this child to your lab!<br /> <b>Bone Gnawer: </b>Guys? While you guys were all arguing, the Black Spiral Dancers just kidnapped the child.<br /> <b>Black Spiral Dancers:</b> *Car Tires squealing as they drive away*<br /> <b>Fianna: </b> Told you the thing would fall to the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Okay maybe not so funny, but it amused me and in the end that is all that matters. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 04-25-2017, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:49:45-07:00","id":1083586,"title":"","content":"I think it is funny- l laughed at the Glasswalker and Fianna characterizations!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:55:51-07:00","id":1083591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083586#post1083586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is funny- l laughed at the Glasswalker and Fianna characterizations!</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I was afraid I didn't do some of the tribes characterizations justice. But Glasswalker and Fianna were easy to come with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T12:54:31-07:00","id":1083624,"title":"","content":"There are really not that many Metis though. I use the 1:500,000 ratio for the population of the Garou Nation, so there might be 15,000 Garou in the Garou Nation by my reckoning (I am not including any Garou outside the Garou Nation in my numbers). Of that number, I figure that 88% are probably Homid, 11% are probably Lupus (keeping the 8:1 ratio from the Core), and 1% are probably Metis because the social stigma of having sex with other Garou is so great. Accidental Metis are really uncommon, the mother has to get pregnant before one of the parents experiences the First Change, so Metis should be uncommon because few Garou are stupid enough to get it on with another Garou, especially since there are plenty of willing and eager Kinfolk around. In all, there should be 150 Metis in the Garou Nation by my reckoning.<br /> <br /> When you look at the incidence of fertile female mules (there is no evidence of any fertile male mules in history), there are around sixty record cases in the past five hundred years. During that time, there were a total of 6 billion mules born in the world, so that means a 1:50,000,000 occurrence of fertile female miles. I doubt that there have been enough female Metis born in the last fifty thousand years to reach even one percent of that number. Just a thought...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:39:30-07:00","id":1083697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083624#post1083624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are really not that many Metis though. I use the 1:500,000 ratio for the population of the Garou Nation, so there might be 15,000 Garou in the Garou Nation by my reckoning (I am not including any Garou outside the Garou Nation in my numbers). Of that number, I figure that 88% are probably Homid, 11% are probably Lupus (keeping the 8:1 ratio from the Core), and 1% are probably Metis because the social stigma of having sex with other Garou is so great. Accidental Metis are really uncommon, the mother has to get pregnant before one of the parents experiences the First Change, so Metis should be uncommon because few Garou are stupid enough to get it on with another Garou, especially since there are plenty of willing and eager Kinfolk around. In all, there should be 150 Metis in the Garou Nation by my reckoning.<br /> <br /> When you look at the incidence of fertile female mules (there is no evidence of any fertile male mules in history), there are around sixty record cases in the past five hundred years. During that time, there were a total of 6 billion mules born in the world, so that means a 1:50,000,000 occurrence of fertile female miles. I doubt that there have been enough female Metis born in the last fifty thousand years to reach even one percent of that number. Just a thought...</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually agree with this entirely.<br /> <br /> And who knows, the Perfect Metis prophecy could entirely being this infinitesimally small chance occurrence happening. That's kind of how things go anyways.<br /> Outside of that explanation though, if I were to do a random fertile Metis storyline, I think it would have to be outside of a modern times game. The event has so much spiritual baggage that comes with it, I couldn't see doing a random false birth random event so close to the Apocalypse and giving it no greater meaning. That just seems like bad storytelling within the setting as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:53:16-07:00","id":1083702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083697#post1083697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually agree with this entirely.<br /> <br /> And who knows, the Perfect Metis prophecy could entirely being this infinitesimally small chance occurrence happening. That's kind of how things go anyways.<br /> Outside of that explanation though, if I were to do a random fertile Metis storyline, I think it would have to be outside of a modern times game. The event has so much spiritual baggage that comes with it, I couldn't see doing a random false birth random event so close to the Apocalypse and giving it no greater meaning. That just seems like bad storytelling within the setting as written.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking about setting such a story in Wyld West.<br /> <br /> Metis comes over to America from Europe with Kinfolk Siblings and passes as Homid. &quot;Fate&quot; intervenes, &quot;punishes&quot; her trickery, and she falls pregnant. (If I was a metis and I found myself pregnant, I'd freak the fuck out. &quot;What the fuck is in me?!?!&quot;) Has a perfectly normal human son that goes though his first change. Son has no clue his mother is metis. The Kinfolk Siblings hide/cremate their sister's body and the Galliards remember the Metis as Homid and founder of a high pure breed bloodline.<br /> <br /> Lots of drama when the whole mess comes to light generations later.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I don't know how feasible it is for a Garou to hide their breed. I just wanted to play with the idea of immigrants coming over to America and redefining themselves.<br /> <br /> ((I considered briefly using this idea for my quest, but decided to keep with &quot;Female Get of Fenris comes over from America to start a new life without all the sexist bullshit she put up with at her European Sept.&quot;))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 04-25-2017, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:10:37-07:00","id":1083708,"title":"","content":"Well, one possible scenario would be a cuckoo's egg, where the child was actually a frectori (one capable of hiding their Wyrm scent) implanted by a Breeder Bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T15:41:10-07:00","id":1083725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083702#post1083702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was thinking about setting such a story in Wyld West.<br /> <br /> Metis comes over to America from Europe with Kinfolk Siblings and passes as Homid. &quot;Fate&quot; intervenes, &quot;punishes&quot; her trickery, and she falls pregnant. (If I was a metis and I found myself pregnant, I'd freak the fuck out. &quot;What the fuck is in me?!?!&quot;) Has a perfectly normal human son that goes though his first change. Son has no clue his mother is metis. The Kinfolk Siblings hide/cremate their sister's body and the Galliards remember the Metis as Homid and founder of a high pure breed bloodline.<br /> <br /> Lots of drama when the whole mess comes to light generations later.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I don't know how feasible it is for a Garou to hide their breed. I just wanted to play with the idea of immigrants coming over to America and redefining themselves.<br /> <br /> ((I considered briefly using this idea for my quest, but decided to keep with &quot;Female Get of Fenris comes over from America to start a new life without all the sexist bullshit she put up with at her European Sept.&quot;))</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Some ShadowLord Homid suceeded in passing as a lupus in the Red Talon Tribe Book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T16:13:45-07:00","id":1083740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083564#post1083564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to explain my thought process behind why I created this topic and maybe include a funny story.<br /> <br /> A while ago, I saw a topic about a Metis in a romantic relationship with a Mage. Me being a weirdo with an interest in biology wondered &quot;What does a Male Metis semen look like? Are male Metis shooting blanks? Malformed sperm? Sperm that just doesn't recognize human/lupus ovum as a viable destination?&quot; My mind wanders to strange places.<br /> <br /> So I did some research. While Metis aren't mules, they do share the infertility trait with them. I discovered male Mules don't produce sperm at all because of a chromosome mismatch inhibiting the meiosis processes. I doubt the metis has the same exact issue, but its close enough for game psuedo-science. &quot;Cool, let's steal metis shooting blanks in case the question does come up in game.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then I read about Female Mules producing foals. It's a pretty rare event. So rare in countries with a less educated population, they are considered omens. Kind of like how the perfect metis is considered an Omen.<br /> <br /> So, while I agree the general game setting doesn't need any metis producing offspring, the idea of female metis rarely producing offspring may be good story fodder. I would never have a PC metis be fertile. Removing infertility would remove a large part of being metis. I doubt female metis are getting loving any due to the social stigma of metis. The offspring being a product of Rape is a subject I rather not touch upon here. Maybe the Black Spiral Dancers have more incidents of this which would lead to the occasional unholy jihad to bring about the apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Any who, I created this topic to brainstorm the Garou Nation's reaction to such events. After a couple of false &quot;Perfect Metis&quot; maybe most Garou discount the actual Perfect Metis. Others could just want to outright kill the offspring. A few true believes may begin to sharpen their claws and klaives in preparation for the upcoming battle. I should disclose I am Agnostic, so religions assigning conflicting meanings to rare and random events intrigues me. My games trend more political, so the Garou arguing over how to react to this &quot;miracle&quot; is good story fodder at my table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metis sterility is spiritually-rooted, much like how conceiving and gestating a metis requires a shapeshifter mother with Rage and any attempt to clone a metis fails automatically. Hybrid infertility is not really the place to go looking for the mechanism or model, particularly when you consider how the breed often resembles something other than a wolf, with the potential to have horns, scales, hooves, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T19:17:42-07:00","id":1083782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083740#post1083740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Metis sterility is spiritually-rooted, much like how conceiving and gestating a metis requires a shapeshifter mother with Rage and any attempt to clone a metis fails automatically. Hybrid infertility is not really the place to go looking for the mechanism or model, particularly when you consider how the breed often resembles something other than a wolf, with the potential to have horns, scales, hooves, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div> With a few exceptions from Rage Across the World, theirs spontaneous Metis there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T22:26:54-07:00","id":1083852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083782#post1083782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a few exceptions from Rage Across the World, theirs spontaneous Metis there...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Chernobyl Exclusion Zone is hardly a typical case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T04:47:11-07:00","id":1083916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083852#post1083852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Chernobyl Exclusion Zone is hardly a typical case.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know... and its worth noting that kinfolk mothers inevitably die.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T21:19:22-07:00","id":1084316,"title":"","content":"Why not have the children of the fertile metis' be part of a pack with the perfect metis as the alpha. I have a homebrew all metis and children of metis tribe, with kin-folk in the disability activism community, that basically started that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:39:02-07:00","id":1084562,"title":"","content":"I run it in my games thus:<br /> <br /> Every few centuries, rumors circulate concerning a 'metis birth'. Then the rumors slowly die away. Ten to twenty years later, long after the 'metis birth' furor has died down and been forgotten, a powerful new Black Spiral Dancer makes an appearance is a place faaaar away from where this metis pregnancy is said to've happened.<br /> <br /> Metis are spiritually and physically incapable of conceiving. The Wyrm, however, sometimes 'blesses' metis in ways the Garou Nation find horrifying.<br /> <br /> The Perfect Metis? The one in Rage Across the Heavens is merely the first <i>confirmed</i> metis birth. There have been others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-02T07:19:17-07:00","id":1086616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1083697#post1083697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]I couldn't see doing a random false birth random event so close to the Apocalypse and giving it no greater meaning. That just seems like bad storytelling within the setting as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can use it as fodder for a &quot;the world is dieing and this is but one of its spasms&quot; line in a modern game.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:00:53-07:00","id":1091129,"title":"","content":"I personally see the inability of Garou to breed with each-other as a failsafe from Gaia to stop them from exterminating wolves and humans and to give them motivation to care for those species.<br /> \u200bSo, in my opinion, if once in a blue sky a metis would produce an offspring nothing would change and Gaia shouldn't care as species as a whole is not affected. The writers simply went a bit lazy with biology.<br /> \u200bOn the other hand a mage with Life and Spirit could wreck so much havoc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:09:30-07:00","id":1091133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1091129#post1091129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally see the inability of Garou to breed with each-other as a failsafe from Gaia to stop them from exterminating wolves and humans and to give them motivation to care for those species.<br /> \u200bSo, in my opinion, if once in a blue sky a metis would produce an offspring nothing would change and Gaia shouldn't care as species as a whole is not affected. The writers simply went a bit lazy with biology.<br /> \u200bOn the other hand a mage with Life and Spirit could wreck so much havoc...</div> </div> </div> </div>The Revised Storyteller's Handbook basically laid out that where Mage says &quot;I can definitely help you with...&quot; in regards to any problems with breeding, Werewolf's answer is &quot;Nooooope,&quot; Right down to how the rules are set up, in fact. Said Mage is required to have Occult 6+ in order to possibly discern where anything comes from and requires impossible timing in a place where Garou would tear them to shreds present right at conception in order to try anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T08:55:26-07:00","id":1091153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1083179-female-mule-fertility-and-the-perfect-metis?p=1091133#post1091133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Revised Storyteller's Handbook basically laid out that where Mage says &quot;I can definitely help you with...&quot; in regards to any problems with breeding, Werewolf's answer is &quot;Nooooope,&quot; Right down to how the rules are set up, in fact. Said Mage is required to have Occult 6+ in order to possibly discern where anything comes from and requires impossible timing in a place where Garou would tear them to shreds present right at conception in order to try anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSure. That's the answer you can give to Justify any &quot;Nooooopes&quot;, so players don't fuck with other game lines. Although, Occult 6 is very easy to achieve, just get some Dream and Past Lives backgrounds as a simplest solution. You can get even higher with that and add some Mind augmentation for max hax. Being &quot;present at conception&quot; is quite easy to solve in modern times.<br /> <br /> You can also go forward and see what sort of strangeness comes out of dozens of successes of fertility magic. With that I don't mean a result of 'normal' Garou by any means. I said 'Havoc' not &quot;Solve beastman reproductive issues&quot;.<br /> <br /> though you can involve a mage NPC ready to give 1 time fertility charm for some serious service as a story hook. If it will work as intended is another question altogether.<br /> <br /> \u200bBTW. can you tell me where you got that info? Just curious, would like to read myself. As in page or chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 05-11-2017, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T09:29:12-07:00","id":1091165,"title":"","content":"And this is EXACTLY why you aren't supposed to talk to mages...Though I can see this (coupled with horrible spiritual consequences) as setting for a cautionary tale about mages...<br /> <br /> And, while I cannot speak for Saur Ops, I guess the Occult 6+ it's because this is what takes to know enough about Cainites to lift the Curse of Caine in the mage section of Vampire Storytellers Handbook (coupled with Prime 6 and a lot of Spheres at high levels). I think extrapolating the required knowledge about leeches with the knowledge about the spiritual ties of the Garou needed to understand the metis condition it's not a bad idea.<br /> <br /> In that book it's also mentioned that among those likely to know so much about vampires are the Nephandi...and I would say that's the same in this case. Malfean Nephandi are more likely know about the ancestral enemies (and sometimes servants) of their God than most Dreamspeakers, and such a potent and knowledgeable Nephandi can probably mask his &quot;wyrm smell&quot;, vanish the Banes that are constantly following him, and be very gentle too...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-11-2017, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T09:42:57-07:00","id":1091174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcod